# Glossary of Terms and Abbreviations

This glossary provides standardized definitions for all abbreviations, KPIs, and business terms used across the Analytics Use Case Library.  
It ensures a consistent understanding between business users, data engineers, and report developers.

---

## 1. General Terms

| Term | Definition | Notes |
|------|-------------|-------|
| **UC** | Use Case | Unique analytical scenario documented as a one-pager. |
| **KPI** | Key Performance Indicator | Quantitative metric used to measure performance. |
| **Δ (Delta)** | Absolute variance | Difference in value vs Plan, LY, or Target. |
| **Δ% (Delta Percent)** | Relative variance | Percentage difference vs Plan, LY, or Target. |
| **3-30-300** | Analytical design principle | Structure ensuring clarity across Insight (3s), Story (30s), and Detail (300s). |
| **Copilot Readiness** | Documentation and metadata quality standard | Ensures AI tools can interpret KPIs, goals, and relationships. |

---

## 2. Finance and Performance

| Term | Definition | Notes |
|------|-------------|-------|
| **Net Sales Amount** | Revenue excluding returns and taxes. | Measured at invoice line level. |
| **Gross Margin %** | (Net Sales − COGS) / Net Sales. | Expressed as a percentage. |
| **COGS Amount** | Cost of Goods Sold. | Direct costs linked to sold products. |
| **Operating Profit Amount** | EBIT-level profit measure excluding non-operational items. | Calculated after SG&A costs. |
| **Δ Net Sales Amount** | Difference vs Plan or LY in Net Sales. | Currency value. |
| **Δ% Net Sales** | Percentage difference vs Plan or LY. | Relative measure. |
| **Price Realization %** | Actual net price ÷ list price. | Indicates pricing discipline. |
| **Plan** | Approved target for the current fiscal year. | Used as baseline in variance analyses. |
| **LY** | Last Year. | Comparison period. |

---

## 3. Supply Chain and Inventory

| Term | Definition | Notes |
|------|-------------|-------|
| **Inventory Days** | Average days of stock coverage. | Derived from stock value ÷ daily COGS. |
| **DSO (Days Sales Outstanding)** | Average collection period for receivables. | Shorter is better. |
| **DPO (Days Payables Outstanding)** | Average payment term for payables. | Longer is better for liquidity. |
| **CCC (Cash Conversion Cycle)** | DSO + Inventory Days − DPO. | Measures working capital efficiency. |
| **OTIF** | On-Time In-Full delivery. | Supplier service quality metric. |
| **Stock-out Rate %** | Share of demand not fulfilled due to missing stock. | Used to monitor service levels. |

---

## 4. Customer and Market

| Term | Definition | Notes |
|------|-------------|-------|
| **Retention %** | Share of customers retained over a period. | Opposite of churn. |
| **Churn %** | Share of customers lost during a period. | Complement to Retention %. |
| **CLV (Customer Lifetime Value)** | Discounted gross margin contribution per customer over lifetime. | Used for profitability analysis. |
| **NPS (Net Promoter Score)** | Survey-based loyalty indicator. | Measured from customer feedback. |
| **Campaign ROI %** | Return on marketing spend. | (Incremental GM − Campaign Cost) ÷ Campaign Cost. |

---

## 5. Procurement and Cost

| Term | Definition | Notes |
|------|-------------|-------|
| **PPV (Purchase Price Variance)** | Difference between actual and contracted purchase prices. | Expressed as %. |
| **Rebid** | Renewal or renegotiation of supplier terms. | Action code PC2. |
| **Indexation** | Linking prices to indices (e.g., FX or commodity). | Reduces volatility. |

